aced piece\n3. If White trades knight for bishop, it removes their strong central piece\n4. If the knight retreats, I've gained time for development\n5. The bishop on e6 also controls important central squares\n\nThis move combines development with immediate tactical pressure, which is ideal in the opening/early middlegame.\n\nAnswer: B: c8-e6"}
