.\n\nReason: Capturing the knight on d5 with my bishop accomplishes multiple goals: (1) eliminates White's best-placed piece that controls key squares around my king, (2) opens the d-file potentially for my queen, (3) simplifies the position when I'm behind in development, and (4) removes a piece that could support White's attack. This is a principled move that addresses the immediate threat.\n\nAnswer: B: e6-d5"}
